course: dictionary
lesson: 14190
title: Mortality
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mortality means the fact that every living thing will one day die. People, dogs, trees and birds all have mortality, because none of them live forever. «Reading about the old king made Sam think about his own mortality.» The words think about and his own tell you that mortality here means Sam, like every living thing, will one day die.
explain: Mortality can also be a number. It means how many deaths happen in a group or a place over a time, and this is often called the mortality rate. «The mortality rate in the town fell after the new clean water pipes were built.» The word fell tells you the number of deaths went down.
explain: Some phrases use mortality in a set way. «Infant mortality» means babies dying young. «Human mortality» means the mortality of people. «Face your own mortality» means think seriously that your own life will end one day. When you see the word, check the words around it to find out which meaning is used.
fact: Mortality means the fact that every living thing will one day die.
fact: Mortality can also mean the number of deaths in a group, place or time, often called the mortality rate.
fact: «Infant mortality» means babies dying young.
fact: «Infant mortality» fell a lot because of clean water and vaccines.
fact: «Face your own mortality» means thinking seriously that your own life will end one day.
exercise: «The mortality rate in the town fell after the new clean water pipes were built.» What does mortality rate mean here? | *The number of deaths in the town over a time | The number of people who live in the town | The number of trees in the park | The price of water
exercise: «Reading about the old king made Sam think about his own mortality.» What does mortality mean here? | A kind of music | *The fact that Sam, like every living thing, will one day die | How fast Sam can run | Sam's favourite book
exercise: Which phrase means babies dying young? | *Infant mortality | Human mortality | Clean water pipes | A vaccine
test: «Scientists study infant mortality to find out how to keep babies safe.» What does infant mortality mean? | Babies sleeping a lot | Babies moving to new homes | *Babies dying young | Babies learning to talk
test: Which is the best meaning of mortality? | *The fact that every living thing will one day die | A kind of cloud | A big city | A type of sport
exam: Mira reads that «infant mortality» fell a lot because of clean water and vaccines. What is one thing that helped it fall? | Bigger houses | Babies sleeping more | Longer days | *Clean water
